// fixture-440 (rfc-resolution-semantics.md §3 Axis W — W1): Axis A folded
// into a workspace. Two members (alpha, beta) each require the SAME git dep
// at the SAME url+ref. Per spec/resolver-semantics.md §11 (multi-root BFS,
// one shared lock), that dep is one shared graph node — resolved (and its
// declared version derived) ONCE, not per-member.
//
// lib-shared is pinned to the version-shaped tag "v0.6.0" (no milpa.kdl/
// .nimble version field present, so declared_version_for's step 3 — the
// A3 git-tag fallback — is what produces the version). The expected lock
// carries exactly ONE "lib-shared" dep block with version "0.6.0" and
// declared_version_source "tag" — proving the derivation happened once for
// the whole workspace, not twice (once per requiring member).
workspace {
    member "alpha"
    member "beta"
}
